course: dictionary
lesson: 12610
title: Discovered: found or found out
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Discovered is the past form of discover. It has two main meanings. The first is finding something for the first time, or finding something that was hidden or not known about. «Maya discovered a secret door behind the bookcase.» Nobody knew the door was there until Maya found it.
explain: The second meaning is found out or learned a fact. «Tom discovered that the bus was late every Monday.» Tom did not find a thing. He learned something true, so discovered means found out here.
explain: To check which meaning fits, swap in found or learned and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Discover is the present form, discovered is the past form, and discovering is the -ing form.
fact: «Scientists discovered penicillin in 1928.» They found something new that nobody had known about before.
fact: In maths, pupils can discover a pattern by looking closely at numbers and noticing what repeats.
fact: Explorers discovered new lands, although people often already lived there, so the land was new only to the explorers.
fact: Discovered can mean found, found out, or learned, depending on the sentence.
exercise: «The children discovered a hidden cave behind the waterfall.» What does discovered mean here? | Painted a picture | *Found something hidden | Lost a favourite toy | Ran away quickly
exercise: «Priya discovered that the library closes at five on Fridays.» What did Priya do? | Lost her library card | *Found out a fact | Moved a heavy table | Found a hidden cave
exercise: «Ben looked at the old map and discovered a path through the forest.» Find and copy one word that is a past form of discover. | *discovered | map | forest | path
test: «Scientists discovered a new planet through their telescope.» What does discovered mean? | Bought something from a shop | *Found something for the first time | Forgot something important | Heard a noise
test: «Sam discovered a pattern in the numbers: each one was double the last.» Which meaning fits? | Painted something | Found something hidden | Ran away | *Found out a fact
exam: «Explorers discovered the island, but families had lived there for centuries.» Which word shows that people already lived on the island? | Explorers | island | *lived | discovered
